<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS4" title="In 5 Discussion ‣ The Discrete Charm of the MLP:Binary Routing of Continuous Signals in Transformer Feed-Forward Layers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.4 </span>The MLP as a Learned Quorum System</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS5" title="In 5 Discussion ‣ The Discrete Charm of the MLP:Binary Routing of Continuous Signals in Transformer Feed-Forward Layers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.5 </span>Connection to Superposition and Polysemy</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS6" title="In 5 Discussion ‣ The Discrete Charm of the MLP:Binary Routing of Continuous Signals in Transformer Feed-Forward Layers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.6 </span>Implications for Linearization</span></a></li>
